  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "Notes:\r\n- α(T) defined as α(T) = α0(T-Tc)\r\n- Free energy, F = α(T)∣ψ∣^2 + β/2 * ∣ψ∣^4\r\n- Free energy is plotted as a function of ∣ψ∣ for 3 temepratures. Plot shows how free energy landscape changes with temperature.\r\n\r\nThe plot shows a phase transition from the normal state (T > Tc) to the superconducting state (T < Tc). At T = Tc, the system is at a critical point and the the free energy landscape is flat near ∣ψ∣ = 0. Below Tc, the non-zero minima of the free energy correspond to the superconducting orfer parameter ∣ψ∣, which grows as the temperature decreases below Tc.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Plot extreme solutions as functions of the temperature *)\r\n\r\nSol[T_] := Piecewise[{ {0, T > Tc}, {Sqrt[-alpha0 (T - Tc)/beta], T <= Tc}}]\r\n\r\n(* Plot the solutions as functions of temperature *)\r\nPlot[\r\n  Sol[T], {T, 0, 2}, \r\n  PlotStyle -> {Thick, Blue}, \r\n  AxesLabel -> {\"T\", \"|ψ|\"}, \r\n  PlotLabel -> \"Order Parameter |ψ| vs Temperature\",\r\n  Exclusions -> None (* Ensures a smooth transition at T = Tc *)\r\n]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
