   ],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "Notes:\r\n- For T < Tc, the non-trivial solution is ∣ψ∣ = sqrt(-α(T)/β)\r\n- For T > Tc, the solution is trivial\r\n\r\nThe plot shows a continuous transition at T = Tc, characteristic of a second-order phase transition. Below Tc, the non-trivial solution represents a superconducting state, where ∣ψ∣ increases as the temperature decreases below Tc. Above, Tc, the system is in normal conducting state, and the only condition is ∣ψ∣ = 0.\r\n\r\nThis is consistent with the Ginzburg-Landau theory of superconductivity.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Exercise 3\r\n\r\nThe Landau theory of phase transitions is based on the idea that the free energy can be expanded as a power series in the order parameter m. For a second order phase transition, the order parameter grows continuously from zero at the phase transition so the first few terms of the power series will hold more 'weight'. If the free energy is expanded to sixth order in the order parameter,\r\n\r\nF = Fn + α|ψ|^2 + β/2|ψ|^4 + γ/3|ψ|^6\r\n\r\nthe system will undergo a first order phase transition if α0 > 0, β < 0, γ > 0.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {},
   "executionSummary": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Define parameters with arbitrary values*)\r\nα0 = 1.5;\r\nβ = -0.2;\r\nγ = 0.1;\r\nTc = 1;  (* Superconducting transition temperature *)\r\n\r\n(* Define alpha as a function of temperature *)\r\nα[T_] := α0 (T - Tc)\r\n\r\n(* Define free energy function *)\r\nF[T_, ψ_] := α[T] ψ^2 + (β/2) ψ^4 + (γ/3) ψ^6\r\n\r\n(* Plot Free Energy for several temperatures *)\r\nPlot[\r\n  Evaluate@Table[F[T, ψ], {T, 1.02, 1.06, 0.009}], \r\n  {ψ, -2, 2}, \r\n  PlotLegends -> Table[\"T = \" <> ToString[T], {T, 1.02, 1.06, 0.01}],\r\n  AxesLabel -> {\"ψ\", \"F\"},\r\n  PlotLabel -> \"Free Energy for several Temperatures\",\r\n  PlotRange -> {{-2,2},{-0.09, 0.09}}\r\n]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
